        "original_id": "8d57edeb-674f-5499-9e48-db2bc8439382",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ernest Whitington\n- Roles: journalist, columnist\n- Organizations: South Australian Register, The Advertiser\n- Projects: \"Out among the People\"\n- Events: newspaper amalgamation, publication history\n\nFacts:\n- The South Australian Register was first published in London in June 1836.\n- Ernest Whitington was born around 1873 and was known to his friends as \"Ern.\"\n- Ernest Whitington was a journalist in South Australia.\n- Ernest Whitington wrote the popular \"Out among the People\" column under the name \"Rufus\" in the Register and later in The Advertiser after the two newspapers were amalgamated.\n- The South Australian Register folded in February 1931, nearly a century after its first publication.\n- Ernest Whitington died on 13 April 1934.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
